<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Containers on Sidnei Weber</title><link>https://sidneiweber.com.br/tags/containers/</link><description>Recent content in Containers on Sidnei Weber</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>pt-br</language><copyright>© 2026 Sidnei Weber</copyright><lastBuildDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://sidneiweber.com.br/tags/containers/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Docker: qual a diferença entre ADD e COPY (e quando usar cada um)</title><link>https://sidneiweber.com.br/diferenca-entre-docker-add-e-copy/</link><pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://sidneiweber.com.br/diferenca-entre-docker-add-e-copy/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Se você já escreveu um &lt;code&gt;Dockerfile&lt;/code&gt;, provavelmente já se deparou com estas duas instruções:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-dockerfile" data-lang="dockerfile"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;COPY&lt;/span&gt; app.py /app/&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;e:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-dockerfile" data-lang="dockerfile"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;ADD&lt;/span&gt; app.py /app/&lt;span class="err"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;À primeira vista, parecem fazer exatamente a mesma coisa. E, na maioria dos casos simples, realmente fazem. Mas existe uma diferença importante:&lt;/p&gt;</description><media:content xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="https://sidneiweber.com.br/diferenca-entre-docker-add-e-copy/feature-image.png"/></item></channel></rss>